title\": \"Changed Premise\",\n   \"type\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"affected_uses\": {\n   \"description\": \"Saved investigation, experiment or interpretation IDs using the changed premise directly or through recorded knowledge revisions; never inferred from similar words\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"string\"\n   },\n   \"title\": \"Affected Uses\",\n   \"type\": \"array\"\n  }\n },\n \"required\": [\n  \"kind\",\n  \"statement\",\n  \"conditions\",\n  \"source_ids\"\n ],\n \"title\": \"KnowledgeUpdate\",\n \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n--- CE ---\n0 : RestoreCommittedLogs is not part of DefaultConfig (config.go:329-341 leaves it false), and with the option disabled restoreFromCommittedLogs returns immediately (api.go:725-727), so default-configured nodes cannot reach the blocked path.\n1 : A snapshot at or near the commit index removes the replay entirely: parsed index 3 in receipt d61420dbc49a4072937b040aac55a51c and the short case of receipt 7ee579ae94bd4812beaa21ce1ca9bb2e restarted real prefixes with a small enough tail that NewRaft returned, so snapshot cadence bounds exposure to this path.\n2 : A larger MaxAppendEntries moves the boundary: parsed index 5 of receipt 87aea51bbd8a4b579f138f2c4986343a completed the very state that hangs at the default batch size, so a deployment that raises MaxAppendEntries enough for 128*MaxAppendEntries to cover its snapshot lag does not encounter the block.\n3 : The trigger observations are bounded windows, now including a thirty-second one in receipt fd88bc508e4f413393838b7d64657137, but still finite runs; permanence is claimed from the source-level absence of any consumer before NewRaft returns, from shutdownCh having no closer outside Shutdown on the returned *Raft, and from the blocked case outlasting the 128-batch control's five-millisecond completion by four orders of magnitude.\n4 : No incorrect commit, applied entry, vote or membership decision was observed in any case; the evidence contradicts only startup progress.